@prefix pm:      <https://pajew.ski/prima-materia/ontology#> .
@prefix pmc:     <https://pajew.ski/prima-materia/concepts/> .
@prefix rdfs:    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix skos:    <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#> .

#
# prima-materia — the rule that falls on the saying rather than on the doing
#
# One generalization, formed on 2026-09-23 out of two witnesses that the same
# run put side by side and three more that the counter-search brought back.
# The two are Chinese, of the same century, and independent of one another: a
# swindler's instruction reported as fraud by Ge Hong, and the same device
# stated as doctrine in the foundational document of the Celestial Masters.
#
# It is not another copy of generalizations/no-failed-run-counts.ttl and the
# difference is one step. That statement is about where a transmission puts an
# empty run. This one is about a class of rules that do not dispose of the run
# at all: they fall on the practitioner's account of it, and they make the
# saying itself the fault, the cause of the failure, or the proof against the
# speaker.
#
# The counter-search against the holding was carried before the statement was
# written, as SPEC §16 requires. It did not refute it. It returned three
# further witnesses and, more usefully, four transmissions that do the
# opposite, and the statement is worded so that the class is a recurring
# device and not a rule of the material.
#

pmc:TheRuleAgainstReportingTheAbsence a pm:Generalizing ;
    rdfs:label "The rule falls on saying that nothing happened, not on the nothing"@en, "Die Regel trifft das Sagen, dass nichts geschah, nicht das Nichts"@de ;
    pm:generalizedStatement "A recurring minority device in operative transmissions attaches a consequence not to a failed performance but to the practitioner's report that the result did not come. The consequence takes one of three forms: the saying is made the cause of the failure it would report, so that a man who says he is not cured has thereby forfeited the cure; the saying is made an offence in its own right, with a penalty stated in the same register as the transmission's other penalties; or the saying is made evidence about the speaker, so that the doubt is read as a fault in him rather than as information about the procedure. In every instance the rule stands in the operative text and not in a later gloss, and it operates on the one report that a transmission of this kind could be held against. In this holding on 2026-10-17 it stood in eight of the 107 transmissions entered beyond their registration, in at least six languages from the fourth century to the twentieth; the figure counts what has been harvested and is a lower bound."@en ;
    pm:generalizedFrom pmc:GehongMaShi, pmc:CmYanhuiWuyi, pmc:SteinerSchweigeGebot, pmc:WhatMayBeDoubtedAndWhatMayNot, pmc:WaterQuestionCaution, pmc:TurbaExemplumRelinquentis, pmc:RasarnavaSastraDusanaAtmadosa, pmc:AgrippaCulpaLectoris, pmc:TurbaCulpaInOperante ;
    skos:note "Rewritten on 2026-10-17 after the protocol at examinations/the-rule-against-reporting-the-absence-tested.ttl. The statement began: A recurring device in operative transmissions attaches a consequence not to a failed performance but to the practitioner's report that the result did not come; and it ended with the sentence on the one report a transmission could be held against. The protocol met the statement's own second falsifier, a small minority, and the word minority and the rate are the change; the three forms are unchanged. Two witnesses were added by the same protocol, both of the third form: Agrippa's closing rule that the reader who fails is not to say the author lied but to accuse himself, and the Turba's blame not the Wise but yourselves."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:compilerInference ;
    skos:note "A seventh witness added on 2026-10-11 from the Rasārṇava, paṭala 18, verses 186 to 193, and it is the first of the seven that quotes the forbidden saying instead of forbidding it. The six before it operate on an utterance from outside: the saying causes the failure, the saying is an offence, the saying is evidence about the speaker, or the reading that would precede the saying is foreclosed. This one puts the utterance in the operator's mouth in direct speech — he tells all creatures, I have no accomplishment in the elixir — and then supplies, also in his voice, the three accounts he would give of it: that the accomplishment was only in the mind, that the toil was his own, that the loss of materials was his own and done by a bad wit. All three are then refused in the work's voice: such a one does not know that what he did was done without the rule, and the most sinful blames the treatise and does not find the fault in himself. The device is the same and the form is one step further on, because a man who has had this result finds his own words already printed and already answered."@en ;
    skos:note "The statement is not widened for it, and the reason is that the Rasārṇava case supplies a consequence of the first form and not a fourth form. The loss is assigned to invisible agents who carry the eaten mercury off and leave ash in the hand, and the operator's own report is made the proof that he departed from the rule; the chapter closes by putting the condition of success in Śiva's being pleased. So it falls under the third form — the saying is evidence about the speaker — with the first form's mechanism attached. What it adds to the class is strength and not extent."@en ;
    skos:note "The counter-search for this witness was carried against the holding before it was added, as SPEC §16 requires, and it came back with the sharpest counter-case the statement has yet had, inside the same work. Eighty verses earlier, at 18.136-143, the Rasārṇava states a condition of failure of exactly the kind this device is supposed to displace: a sign-set of some twenty-seven bodily signs of undigested mercury, two counter-draughts by name, and the sentence that if it still does not digest he dies, there is no doubt of it. That passage says nothing about reporting and nothing about the operator's standing, and it is held at pmc:RasarnavaRasajirnalaksana. The counter-search also returned the Chinese case of the seven men ruined by the drug at examinations/elixir-deaths.ttl, where a transmission's own literature records the outcome against the drug and names the dead. So the statement survives, and what the counter-search establishes is narrower and more useful than a survival: one chapter of one work carries the device and its opposite a few pages apart, which rules out the reading that a transmission carrying this device is thereby incapable of stating a checkable failure."@en ;
    skos:note "A sixth witness added on 2026-09-26 from the Turba philosophorum, Dictum 27, and it is a variant of the third form rather than a plain instance, which is why the difference is stated here. The three forms this statement names all operate on an utterance: the saying causes the failure, the saying is an offence, the saying is evidence about the speaker. The Turba's case operates on an inference and an act. Gregorius reports a man who, when the redness was somewhat slow in appearing, imagined that he had made a mistake and so relinquished the work; the work records the inference as his error and the loss as his own, and the sentence immediately after it tells the reader that the redness does not delay in coming. Nothing is said about reporting anything. What is closed off is the reading of a delay as information, which is the same result reached one step earlier: a man who may not take the absence for a fact has nothing to report."@en ;
    skos:note "The Turba case also shows the device without the penalty, and that is worth separating. The other five witnesses attach something to the utterance — a forfeited cure, a stated penalty, a fault found in the speaker. This one attaches nothing and needs nothing: the loss is supplied by the transmission's own assurance that the redness was on its way. A successor statement will have to decide whether the class is defined by the consequence or by the reading it forecloses, and this witness is the case that forces the question."@en ;
    skos:note "The two that carry the first form, and they are the reason the statement was written. A fourth-century Chinese report of a fraud at Xinggu quotes the operative rule word for word: though you are not cured at once, tell people that you are cured, and you will certainly be cured; but if you tell anybody that you are not yet cured, then in the end you will never be cured — such is the law of the Way, and you must not fail to trust it. The chapter then records what the rule produced: those who came later asked those who had come before, the earlier ones always said they were cured, none dared say he was not, and within ten days the operator was immensely rich. The admonitions of the Celestial Masters, of the same century and a different transmission, state the second form as doctrine: one who on meeting calamity says that serving the Dao is of no benefit thereby commits an offence of three thousand, and an earlier passage of the same work says that a man who does not blame himself but cries out that serving the Dao is of no benefit deepens his transgression by it."@en ;
    skos:note "The pairing is what makes the two worth more than either. One transmission states the device as its own rule; a contemporary outside the other describes an identical device as a swindle and names the man who ran it. The graph therefore holds the same construction under both descriptions, from the same century and the same language area, without either text depending on the other. It is not a claim that the one transmission is the other's fraud, and nothing here says so."@en ;
    skos:note "The three the counter-search added, each carrying a different form. The anthroposophical course puts the pupil's result under a rule of silence — be silent about your spiritual sights, indeed be silent about them even before yourself — after printing in advance the colours he is to see; the one act by which a perception could be compared with another pupil's or held against the announced colours is the act forbidden, and the prohibition reaches the pupil's own reflection. The Zande corpus states the third form as a ranking: doubt of the charged things and of the practitioners costs nothing, but to scout the power to bewitch or to sneer at the ordeal is held to prove the doubter a witch himself. And the Hekhalot descent attaches its whole penalty at the sixth palace not to a deed but to a question, so that asking about the nature of the water is the failure."@en ;
    skos:note "What the counter-search found on the other side, and it is the half that keeps the statement honest. Four transmissions in this holding do the opposite. A king of Dahomey complains in 1871 before the assembled army that the diviners took his cowries, cattle, slaves and wives and told him many lies, naming the war they promised him and the defeat he got — the client reporting the failure in public, with prediction, outcome and fee. The Zande poison oracle requires the second consultation and makes the validity of the first depend on it, so that the checking question is not forbidden but prescribed. A Kongo witness reports eating the forbidden thing without consequence, which is a member of the transmission reporting a negative result about its own prohibition. And a European blessing corpus admits a case in which the words were used without effect and a physician then cured the same complaint, entered as a case rather than reclassified as the physician's excuse. The device is therefore common and not universal, and a transmission that carries it is not thereby of a kind with the others."@en ;
    skos:note "The distinction to keep, because it is where this statement could be read too widely. A rule of secrecy about the method is not an instance. Transmissions that forbid disclosing the procedure are numerous in this holding and they say nothing about the outcome; what counts here is a rule that falls on the report of what came of it. The anthroposophical case is the near edge — it is a silence about the outcome and reads as a rule of method — and it is included on the ground that the text names the pupil's own formulation of his result as the thing to be suppressed. A run that wanted a narrower class would drop it and keep four."@en ;
    skos:note "Why the device is worth a name of its own rather than a line in the statement about where a failed run is put. Those rules dispose of an outcome and leave the practitioner free to say what happened; this one leaves the outcome alone and closes the channel. The two can therefore be stacked, and in one transmission they are: the Celestial Masters both assign a relapse to the patient's bad character and make the complaint about the absence an offence. Where both are present, a run that produced nothing is explained and the explanation cannot be contradicted by the person it was applied to."@en ;
    skos:note "Falsified by showing that the witnesses are not of one kind — that in each case the rule is against disclosing the method or against public complaint in general, rather than against the report that the result failed to come. The Chinese pair resists that reading because both rules name the content of the forbidden saying and it is in both cases that the thing did not work. Falsified in the other direction, and more cheaply, by a count: if a survey of the operative transmissions in this holding found rules of this shape in a small minority of those that make a checkable promise, the statement would be describing five cases and not a device, and should be withdrawn to a remark about them. That count was made on 2026-10-17 and met this condition; the statement has been reworded accordingly, see the note on the rewriting."@en ;
    skos:note "Examined on 2026-10-17, examinations/the-rule-against-reporting-the-absence-tested.ttl, state cases with deviation: the witnesses are of one kind, and the device is a minority one. What a protocol would still have to fix is the population of fully harvested works, and the hard part named before the count stays: the device is invisible where it works, so a count of transmissions that wrote it down counts the legible."@en .
